WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.770
From movies to TV, This year has already delivered
a ton of creepy creatures that obviously come

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.960
from the most deviously creative minds in
the biz.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.620
And after seeing these menacing things come
to life on-screen, it's probably a safe bet

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:15.360
that most of us will be losing an unusual
amount of sleep this year as well.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.830
Here are a few of the scariest new monsters
of 2017.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.250
Winslow on The Walking Dead

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:24.210
The Walking Dead's seventh season presented
Jadis and her community, a group of people

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.870
who've relied on garbage to create giant walls
to keep themselves safe.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.619
That in and of itself was weird enough, but
then their pet zombie, Winslow, came into

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:32.619
the picture.

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:34.900
That's a special moment for small-screen scare
history.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.750
Rick, who wanted to gain the favor of Jadis'
crew for his impending battle with Negan,

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:42.230
was thrown into a pit with the spiked, undead
beast and had to find a way to penetrate his

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.320
dangerous helmet to save his own skin.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:47.820
Trouble was, he was decked out with knives
and a helmet reinforced with metal from a

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:48.820
gas tank.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:52.399
So, not only did we find out just how much
Jadis doesn't play around when it comes to

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:56.550
protecting her junkyard life, but we also
got to see just how much of a resourceful

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.289
survivor Rick Grimes really is with his back
against the wall.

00:00:59.289 --> 00:01:00.840
Or, you know, the garbage.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.139
Pennywise from IT

00:01:10.139 --> 00:01:13.810
Kids of the '80s and '90s who watched the
first iteration of Stephen King's IT will

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:18.020
no doubt recall the eerie, sickening feeling
that washed over them whenever Tim Curry’s

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:20.969
Pennywise the Clown arrived to torture the
children of Derry.

00:01:20.969 --> 00:01:25.240
And it looks like this year's revival effort
will be just as terrifying, if the first glimpses

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.799
of the sinister cinematic clown are any indication.

00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:31.959
Unlike Curry's version, there appears to be
less surface humor present in the new Pennywise,

00:01:31.959 --> 00:01:33.450
played by Bill Skarsgard.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.859
What's really going to earn prime placement
in people's' nightmares with this one, though,

00:01:36.859 --> 00:01:40.049
is how grimy this Pennywise seems to be compared
to the last one.

00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:43.799
Plus, there's the return of the red balloon
— that image alone is enough to induce a

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:46.399
shudder from an entire generation of horror
fans.

00:01:46.399 --> 00:01:48.819
Kong: Skull Island’s lizard monster

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:52.800
Three tongues, countless teeth, and a grunt-scream
that sounds like a velociraptor?

00:01:55.189 --> 00:01:56.959
That's a recipe for absolute disaster.

00:01:56.959 --> 00:02:01.359
Kong: Skull Island's resident Skullcrawlers
gave new meaning to the concept of an ancient

00:02:01.359 --> 00:02:06.359
apex predator, as only one mega-gorilla could
survive their systematic slaughter of his

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.649
species: King Kong.

00:02:07.649 --> 00:02:10.979
It's basically the equivalent of what would
happen if the Cloverfield monster mated with

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:15.450
that real-life dino-sized croc that's been
haunting South Carolina golfers this year.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.010
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2’s octo-beast

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:21.900
Thanks to movies like Pirates of the Caribbean:
Dead Man's Chest and Clash of the Titans,

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:25.450
we've certainly encountered our fair share
of Kraken-like beasts in movies past.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:29.450
But what Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2 pulled
off is something particularly awful.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:33.030
The gang goes toe to toe with this toothy
space octopus monstrosity.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:34.930
And Drax does it with just a pair of daggers.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:36.989
That's a fight fit for a Destroyer, right?

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:41.180
As he leaps in to take on the tentacled creature,
yet another layer of gums open up to receive

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:44.290
him and it's a just whole 'nother level of
nope.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:45.769
Calvin from Life

00:02:45.769 --> 00:02:49.040
When are our fictional friends gonna just
learn that you can't go playing with alien

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:52.239
life-forms and expect things to go well for
anyone involved?

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:55.569
Like a lot of outer space thrillers, when
these International Space Station astronauts

00:02:55.569 --> 00:02:58.680
actually discover Martian life, things are
not what they seem.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:02.569
What begins as a cute little shimmying blob
turns into a full-on intergalactic nightmare

00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:06.930
for everyone onboard, with a creature named
Calvin who can think, feed on almost anything,

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.769
and wants to instinctively destroy for the
sake of its own growth.

00:03:09.769 --> 00:03:13.379
Unlike a lot of on-screen aliens, there's
nothing ridiculous or anthropomorphic about

00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:14.379
this thing.

00:03:14.379 --> 00:03:17.280
It's just plain horrible in a very believable
way.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.519
Ahmanet from The Mummy

00:03:18.519 --> 00:03:22.700
For those who remain skeptical about the Tom
Cruise-led reboot of The Mummy franchise,

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.260
we've got two words for you: Sofia Boutella.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:29.540
The up-and-coming actress portrays an ancient
Egyptian princess named Ahmanet who was entombed

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:34.599
2,000 years ago after murdering her king-father,
then is accidentally resurrected into a power-hungry

00:03:34.599 --> 00:03:38.450
world-wanderer who has no bones about being
an evil empress of darkness.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:41.909
Not only does she have the power to revive
humans to do her deadly bidding, but she's

00:03:41.909 --> 00:03:43.721
also pretty terrible to look at.

00:03:43.721 --> 00:03:47.121
She's got some spooky eye-split maneuver that's
just bound to strike a nerve with anyone who

00:03:47.121 --> 00:03:49.870
uses their own, single-irised eyes to see
it.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.920
Alien: Covenant xenomorphs

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:55.819
With Alien: Covenant, Ridley Scott is returning
to form with his aliens that have tormented

00:03:55.819 --> 00:03:57.269
audiences for decades.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:04:01.410
The footage from this movie hearkens back
to imagery we've seen of these species before.

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:04.000
But there's also some menacing new material
at play, too.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.249
And here we thought the chest-burster from
the original film was peak petrification.

00:04:07.249 --> 00:04:11.400
But, this looks pretty good, too.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.480
Man, talk about a bug on the windshield.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.580
Thanks for watching!

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.829
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:17.829 --> 00:04:20.239
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love too!

